-- title:
--   Supersingular places arise from enhanced supersingular curves
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic a prime $q'$, and let $N \ge 1$ be an integer not divisible by $q'$. Inside the field of Laurent series over $\kappa$ consider the intermediate field $F_N =$ `modularFunctionFieldC κ N`, the $\kappa$-subfield generated by the two series `jqModC κ` and `jqNModC κ N` (the $q$-expansions of $j$ and of its $N$-fold $q$-substitute), and let $w$ be a place of $F_N/\kappa$, that is, a valuation subring of $F_N$ which contains the image of $\kappa$, is not all of $F_N$, and is a principal ideal ring. Assume $w$ lies in `ssPlaces q' N κ`, i.e. $w$ is rational, satisfies the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and the value of $w$ at the element `jGeomGen κ N` lies in the set `ssJSet q' κ`. Then there exist a Weierstrass curve $E$ over $\kappa$ which is elliptic and has no nontrivial $q'$-torsion in $E(\kappa)$ (every $P$ with $q' \cdot P = 0$ is $0$), and an additive subgroup $C \le E(\kappa)$ which is cyclic of cardinality $N$, such that the valuation subring of $w$ is the preimage, under the inclusion of $F_N$ into the full modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFullC κ N` (the $\kappa$-subfield generated by `divisorExpansionsC κ N`), of the valuation subring of the moduli place `moduliPlace κ N E C`.
--
--   This is the surjectivity half of the moduli description of the supersingular locus of $X_0(N)$ in characteristic $q' \nmid N$: every supersingular place of the level-$N$ modular function field is cut out by a pair $(E,C)$ with $E$ supersingular and $C$ cyclic of order $N$. It is used in the construction of the Čerednik–Drinfel'd style bijection between the supersingular places and a class set, and in the computation of decomposition orders at rigid charts.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_toValuationSubring_eq_comap_moduliPlace_of_mem_ssPlaces.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_SSDegeneracyHecke
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_ModuliPlace

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false
open AlgebraicCurve
open ModularCurve

theorem ModularCurve.exists_toValuationSubring_eq_comap_moduliPlace_of_mem_ssPlaces
    {κ : Type} [Field κ] [IsAlgClosed κ] [DecidableEq κ] (q' : ℕ) [Fact q'.Prime] [CharP κ q']
    (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] (hq'N : ¬ q' ∣ N)
    (w : Place κ ↥(modularFunctionFieldC κ N)) (hw : w ∈ ssPlaces q' N κ) :
    ∃ (E : WeierstrassCurve κ) (_ : E.IsElliptic) (_ : ∀ P : E.toAffine.Point, q' • P = 0 → P = 0)
      (C : AddSubgroup E.toAffine.Point) (_ : IsAddCyclic C ∧ Nat.card C = N),
      w.toValuationSubring = (moduliPlace κ N E C).toValuationSubring.comap (IntermediateField.inclusion (modularFunctionFieldC_le_full κ N)).toRingHom := by sorry
